From: ONIE maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] configure: prefer text section placement over ELF image base

Binutils 2.44 accepts --image-base for ELF but includes ELF headers before
.text. GRUB BIOS needs .text at its exact load address. Probe -Ttext first
while preserving --image-base as the alternative for other linkers.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1798,9 +1798,11 @@
 m4_ifndef([AX_CHECK_LINK_FLAG], [m4_fatal([autoconf-archive is missing. You must install it to generate the configure script.])])
 
 if test "x$TARGET_APPLE_LINKER" != x1 ; then
-AX_CHECK_LINK_FLAG([-Wl,--image-base,0x400000],
+dnl GNU ld 2.44 accepts --image-base for ELF too, but that locates the
+dnl ELF headers, not .text. Prefer the section address required by GRUB.
+AX_CHECK_LINK_FLAG([-Wl,-Ttext,0x400000],
+    [TARGET_IMG_BASE_LDOPT="-Wl,-Ttext"],
     [TARGET_IMG_BASE_LDOPT="-Wl,--image-base"],
-    [TARGET_IMG_BASE_LDOPT="-Wl,-Ttext"],
     [],
     [AC_LANG_SOURCE([
 asm (".globl start; start:");
